      "text": "Overview: Date: 14th Nov, 2026 Registrations: Now Open Kickoff Session: 14th Nov (Saturday), 2026 This is a hands-on, build-first hackathon created for individuals who want to launch a real AI product , not just present ideas or mockups. What You’ll Do: During this one day, participants will: Conceptualize, build, and launch a complete agentic AI solution Work on practical, real-world challenges Go through the entire product journey: Identifying the problem Designing system architecture Integrating tools and APIs Delivering a functional end product The core focus is on building AI agents ready for real-world use that can: Think and make decisions. Interact with tools. Execute tasks independently. By the end, you’ll walk away with a working AI product that can be: Added to your portfolio. Demonstrated in interviews. Expanded into real-world use cases. Participation Guidelines: You can join individually or in teams (up to 2 members recommended). All development must happen within the hackathon timeframe. You are free to use AI tools, APIs, and frameworks. Participants must clearly document their process (problem → solution → architecture). A functional prototype or live demo is required. Submission Requirements: A demo video or live working product. Access to the codebase (GitHub or equivalent). A brief explanation of your solution. Rules & Evaluation: ️ Rules: Fully pre-built solutions are not allowed (starter templates are acceptable). Any form of copying or plagiarism will result in disqualification. Teams must clearly specify their actual contribution vs. AI-generated output. Submissions must be fully working products, not just designs or presentations. All entries must be submitted before the deadline.",
