    "details": "<p><strong>Overview:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Date:</strong> 14th Nov, 2026</li>\n<li><strong>Registrations:</strong>&nbsp;Now Open</li>\n<li><strong>Kickoff Session:</strong> 14th Nov (Saturday), 2026</li>\n</ul>\n<p>This is a&nbsp;<strong>hands-on, build-first hackathon</strong>&nbsp;created for individuals who want to&nbsp;<strong>launch a real AI product</strong>, not just present ideas or mockups.</p>\n<p><strong>What You&rsquo;ll Do:</strong></p>\n<p>During this one day, participants will:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Conceptualize, build, and launch a&nbsp;complete agentic AI solution</li>\n<li>Work on&nbsp;practical, real-world challenges</li>\n<li>Go through the entire product journey:\n<ul>\n<li>Identifying the problem</li>\n<li>Designing system architecture</li>\n<li>Integrating tools and APIs</li>\n<li>Delivering a functional end product</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The core focus is on building&nbsp;AI agents ready for real-world use&nbsp;that can:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Think and make decisions.</li>\n<li>Interact with tools.</li>\n<li>Execute tasks independently.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>By the end, you&rsquo;ll walk away with a&nbsp;working AI product&nbsp;that can be:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Added to your portfolio.</li>\n<li>Demonstrated in interviews.</li>\n<li>Expanded into real-world use cases.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Participation Guidelines:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>You can join&nbsp;individually or in teams (up to 2 members recommended).</li>\n<li>All development must happen&nbsp;within the hackathon timeframe.</li>\n<li>You are free to use&nbsp;AI tools, APIs, and frameworks.</li>\n<li>Participants must clearly&nbsp;document their process&nbsp;(problem &rarr; solution &rarr; architecture).</li>\n<li>A&nbsp;functional prototype or live demo is required.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Submission Requirements:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>A&nbsp;<strong>demo video or live working product.</strong></li>\n<li>Access to the&nbsp;<strong>codebase (GitHub or equivalent).</strong></li>\n<li>A brief explanation of your solution.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Rules &amp; Evaluation:</strong></p>\n<p>️&nbsp;<strong>Rules:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Fully pre-built solutions are&nbsp;not allowed&nbsp;(starter templates are acceptable).</li>\n<li>Any form of&nbsp;copying or plagiarism will result in disqualification.</li>\n<li>Teams must clearly specify their actual contribution vs. AI-generated output.</li>\n<li>Submissions must be&nbsp;fully working products, not just designs or presentations.</li>\n<li>All entries must be submitted&nbsp;before the deadline.</li>\n</ul>",
